# component: toggle-group
# decisions: A11Y-20, API-23, DOC-2
# hunks:
#   A11Y-20 (widened 2026-09-24): `orientation` is forwarded to the Base UI group as well as mirrored
#     to `data-orientation`, so a vertical group's arrow keys are up and down. Upstream styles the
#     column and leaves the keys horizontal.
#   API-23: `ToggleGroup` takes `deselectable` (default `true`) and `wrap` (default `false`),
#     both destructured so neither reaches the DOM. `deselectable={false}` wraps `onValueChange`:
#     in single mode (`multiple` is destructured and forwarded unchanged to read it) a change to
#     `[]` is cancelled through Base UI's own `eventDetails.cancel()` before the engine commits it,
#     so the pressed item stays pressed and the caller's `onValueChange` is never called with `[]`,
#     controlled or not. `wrap` writes `data-wrap` and the root gains `data-wrap:flex-wrap` plus,
#     for a joined group, `data-wrap:data-[spacing=0]:gap-y-2`, so the joined borders of two rows
#     never double up. A joined wrapped row starts at an item that is not `:first-child`, which no
#     selector can find, so `useWrappedRowEnds` (a layout effect with a `ResizeObserver` and a
#     child-list `MutationObserver`, active only for `wrap` + `spacing={0}` + horizontal) marks
#     each row's first and last item `data-row-start` / `data-row-end`, and the item gains three
#     classes that give those their rounded ends and the outline variant's leading border. The
#     root's `ref` is merged with the internal one through `mergeRefs` from our npm layer.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file; those hunks carry no decision of their own.
